[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: dns_server
diagnosis_text:
The failure is not in the OSPF/core path but in the DNS service itself. Clients (e.g., host_1_1_1_1) have nameserver 10.200.0.2 configured, and ICMP reachability to the DNS server is healthy (host_1_1_1_1 -> 10.200.0.2 ping succeeds, ~1.6 ms). However, name lookups fail on multiple clients: getent hosts web0.local/web1.local return exit code 2 on both host_1_1_1_1 and host_2_1_1_1, indicating no DNS response. On the dns_server, there are no listeners on TCP/UDP 53 (ss/netstat only show 127.0.0.11 internal stubs), and the DNS daemon is down: named.service is enabled but Active: failed (failed). bind9.service is present but inactive. This explains the symptom: routing is fine, but with named not running, queries to 10.200.0.2 simply fail, so users perceive “DNS unreachable.”

Localization: dns_server node, BIND (named) daemon. Mechanism: resolver points to 10.200.0.2, but no process is bound to port 53, so lookups time out/fail. Root cause: the DNS daemon (named) on dns_server has crashed or failed to start.

Corrective fix: Restart the DNS service on the dns_server: systemctl restart named (and ensure it stays up: systemctl enable named). If a device restart is preferred, rebooting dns_server will also restore service, but a service restart is sufficient. Verify afterwards with getent hosts web0.local/web1.local from clients.
=== END ===